-- title:
--   Reduction is a unit at j=a when a^{q^2}≠ a
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$ and let $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $f$ belong to `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise images of the level-$q$ modular function field $\mathbb Q(\text{divisorExpansions } q)$. Assume: (i) $f$, as a Laurent series, lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red`, the localisation of the subring generated by the constant series from $A$ together with the series `jqModC` and `jqNModC` of level $q$ at the complement of the kernel of reduction; (ii) its image $\bar f$ under `CharPReduction.modularRedLocHom` lies in `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`, the subfield of $k((t))$ generated over $k$ by `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k 1`; (iii) $\bar f\neq 0$. Let $a\in k$ satisfy $a\notin$ `ssJSet q k`, i.e. some elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has a nonzero point killed by $q$, and $a^{q^2}\neq a$. Assume finally that no place $W$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $W.\mathrm{ord}\,f\neq 0$ admits simultaneously $x\in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\,x=a$ and $W.\mathrm{ord}(j-x)>0$, and $y\in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\,y=a^{q}$ and $W.\mathrm{ord}(j_q-y)>0$, where $j$ and $j_q$ denote the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion of $j$ and of its substitution $q\mapsto q^{\,q}$. Then the order of $\bar f$ at the place `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k a`, the place of $k(\bar\jmath)$ corresponding to $\bar\jmath=a$ under the identification with $k(T)$, is $0$.
--
--   This is the case $a^{q^2}\neq a$ of the statement that the reduction modulo $q$ of a function on $X_0(q)_{\overline{\mathbb Q}}$ whose $q$-expansion is regular over $A$ has neither zero nor pole at an ordinary point $\bar\jmath=a$ of the level-one curve in characteristic $q$, provided no zero or pole of the function specialises to the pair $(a,a^q)$ on the Kronecker-congruence model. It is combined with the complementary case $a^{q^2}=a$ in [`ModularCurve.ord_charLGeomPlaceOfPoint_modularRedLocHom_eq_zero_of_not_mem_ssJSet`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ord_charLGeomPlaceOfPoint_modularRedLocHom_eq_zero_of_not_mem_ssJSet).
